  "summary": "A 5-day split with two heavy upper/lower power days (3-5 reps) followed by three bodybuilding-style hypertrophy days that each open with explosive speed sets. Every muscle is trained twice a week, once heavy and once with higher reps and more volume.",
  "evidenceNote": "Weekly volume is high (about 17 sets for back, 15 for quads and 13 for chest per week, not counting speed sets), which sits at or above the upper end of what most hypertrophy research supports, so many lifters will need the author's own advice to drop an accessory per day at first. Twice-weekly frequency and stopping 1-2 reps short of failure on most sets match current evidence; the speed work has little direct hypertrophy evidence behind it, and the article gives no numeric load-progression rule.",
